            <ArticleTitle>Antinociceptive effect of Hyptis pectinata leaves extracts.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>439-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Oral administration of hexanes, chloroform, and ethyl acetate extracts of the leaves of Hyptis pectinata significantly reduced the number of writhing induced by acetic acid and increased the response to thermal stimuli in hot-plate test. Such effect was completely reversed by the opioid antagonist naloxone.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
